            <ArticleTitle>When your patient can't take the stress.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It has been shown that results of adenosine and dipyridamole myocardial scintigraphy are at least equivalent to those provided by conventional treadmill scintigraphy. Therefore, if a patient is unable to achieve a high rate-pressure product by treadmill exercise, that individual should be considered a candidate for pharmacological stress scintigraphy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
